Z||000003||fotofrank||08-17-2000||02:22 PM||||The '84 Fiero and all other Fieros have differant wireing. The '84 is a beast unto it's own. The Haynes manual will help but as they say no cigar. I have an "84 SE and the Popular Mechanics CD that is available at most K-Marts is good to have. You buy the CD with the proper make, modle and year and register on line for the exact car and year you own. Access to good wireing diagrams for you car along with instructions on A?C recharge,paerts replacement and parts locations help a lot. I use mine in conjuntion with a Haynes and Chilton manual. No one source gives me the wholu picture.<BR>To locate a short to ground remove the neg terminal of the battery. Connect a light bulb between the battery neg and the removed wire. now disconnect things till the light goes out. The last thing disconnected is the culpret.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1.html||||reg||11
